 "_doc": "Rule (fixed before any number): MNE's standard montages, each placed in the head frame by its own fiducials (info.set_montage); unit direction vectors from the head origin (the EGI nets sit on a smaller sphere than standard_1005, 0.109 / 0.102 vs 0.114 m, so raw distances mix in a scale offset); an EGI electrode takes an ST name iff they are MUTUAL nearest neighbours in angle and the angle is <= 6 deg (\u2248 1.2 cm on an adult head; the ST grid's nearest-neighbour spacing is \u2248 10.7 deg). ST's synonyms at a shared position (T3/T4/T5/T6 = T7/T8/P7/P8, A1/A2 = M1/M2) are left out of the target set so they cannot split a match. The EGI reference electrode (Cz / VREF, the online reference: flat) is never mapped.",
 "_threshold_deg": 6.0,
